WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.767 --> 00:00:02.935
 Wayne, Mark, congratulations.

00:00:03.035 --> 00:00:04.437
You fellas have made
it into the final round

00:00:04.537 --> 00:00:05.538
of this competition.

00:00:05.605 --> 00:00:07.072
Now we're sending you
back to your home forges

00:00:07.172 --> 00:00:09.809
to recreate an iconic
weapon from history.

00:00:09.876 --> 00:00:11.411
And that weapon is--

00:00:11.478 --> 00:00:14.147
 Show me a falchion.

00:00:14.247 --> 00:00:16.282
WIL WILLIS: --a falchion.

00:00:16.382 --> 00:00:17.417
 Yeah.

00:00:17.484 --> 00:00:18.384
 Ah-ha-ha, yeah.

00:00:18.484 --> 00:00:19.218
 Good luck.

00:00:19.285 --> 00:00:20.086
We'll see you in four days.

00:00:25.124 --> 00:00:26.225 line:7%
 We made it back.

00:00:26.292 --> 00:00:27.627
Welcome to Pirate Forge.

00:00:31.531 --> 00:00:32.632
I've done my research.

00:00:32.699 --> 00:00:35.201
And back in the day, the
armor was getting tougher,

00:00:35.301 --> 00:00:36.903
you know, thicker
leather, introduction

00:00:37.003 --> 00:00:38.171
of chainmail and whatnot.

00:00:38.237 --> 00:00:39.538
So they needed
something that was going

00:00:39.605 --> 00:00:42.007
to cut, and chop with
the strength of an ax

00:00:42.074 --> 00:00:43.943
but still be wielded
like a sword.

00:00:44.010 --> 00:00:46.178
And that's when the
falchion was born.

00:00:46.245 --> 00:00:48.080
My plan for the design
on this, I'm going to go

00:00:48.147 --> 00:00:50.817
with the Damascus pattern.

00:00:50.917 --> 00:00:54.420
What I want to do is make two
solid billets that we draw out,

00:00:54.520 --> 00:00:59.425
cut and restack to make the
one billet for the falchion.

00:00:59.492 --> 00:01:01.161
This is really
taking a long time.

00:01:01.261 --> 00:01:03.563
And this is a lot more work than
I thought it was going to be.

00:01:03.663 --> 00:01:07.300
Hammering out and setting forge
welds on such monster billets,

00:01:07.367 --> 00:01:11.170
I've definitely forgot
how difficult that was.

00:01:11.237 --> 00:01:13.572
I mean, if I would have
used a monostill billet,

00:01:13.639 --> 00:01:15.475
I could have already had
this falchion forged.

00:01:19.078 --> 00:01:20.245 line:0%
MARK: We're here
back in my home forge

00:01:20.345 --> 00:01:22.514 line:7%
in South Burlington, Vermont.

00:01:22.581 --> 00:01:23.316
Boom.

00:01:23.382 --> 00:01:26.953
I think that four days is tight.

00:01:27.053 --> 00:01:29.255
Man, 3/8 cinch is no joke.

00:01:29.355 --> 00:01:31.557
The falchion has this
swell that really

00:01:31.624 --> 00:01:33.025
gives a lot of
forward weight that

00:01:33.092 --> 00:01:34.560
makes it great for chopping.

00:01:34.660 --> 00:01:38.231
So I have to figure out where
I want to put in this swell

00:01:38.331 --> 00:01:40.266
and how to hammer it out.

00:01:40.333 --> 00:01:40.767
So thin.

00:01:43.503 --> 00:01:45.771
I finally get this
swell drawn out.

00:01:45.838 --> 00:01:48.407
And it is just way too thin.

00:01:48.507 --> 00:01:50.076
And I'm not even
close to three inches.

00:01:50.176 --> 00:01:52.178
I'm pretty nervous about
the structural stability

00:01:52.245 --> 00:01:53.746
of what I'm making.

00:01:53.846 --> 00:01:55.081
Ugh.

00:01:55.181 --> 00:01:58.484
So I am just going to
start on a second swell.

00:01:58.584 --> 00:02:02.788
I'm giving up on this flare,
because it's just too thin.

00:02:02.888 --> 00:02:07.159
And I still have enough metal
back here to make it work.

00:02:07.226 --> 00:02:08.560
What I realized is
that the first time,

00:02:08.661 --> 00:02:11.264
I wanted to move the metal
completely horizontally

00:02:11.364 --> 00:02:12.865
from spine to edge.

00:02:12.931 --> 00:02:15.534
And the way that I was doing
it was moving some of the metal

00:02:15.601 --> 00:02:18.170
lengthwise and enough
of the metal lengthwise

00:02:18.237 --> 00:02:20.506
that it just got too thin.

00:02:20.573 --> 00:02:22.308
I put into practice
what I learned

00:02:22.375 --> 00:02:23.642
in making the first swell.

00:02:23.709 --> 00:02:27.212
It's already going a lot
better, a lot faster,

00:02:27.279 --> 00:02:29.248
and getting a lot wider
without getting as

00:02:29.314 --> 00:02:32.084
thin as it did the first time.

00:02:32.184 --> 00:02:33.153
That's it for day one.

00:02:36.723 --> 00:02:37.857 line:7%
WAYNE: It's day two.

00:02:37.924 --> 00:02:39.993 line:0%
Best case scenario, we
get this sucker drawn out.

00:02:40.093 --> 00:02:40.959
We get it quenched.

00:02:41.026 --> 00:02:42.194
It comes out looking great.

00:02:42.294 --> 00:02:43.796
Never quenched a blade
this big, I don't

00:02:43.863 --> 00:02:45.498
know what's going to happen.

00:02:45.565 --> 00:02:48.200
About to make this thing
change into a real sword.

00:02:48.267 --> 00:02:50.636
This is a special
momentous occasion.

00:02:50.736 --> 00:02:54.039
I was so inspired by
this blade I was like,

00:02:54.139 --> 00:02:55.975
there should be a falchion song.

00:02:56.042 --> 00:03:00.613
[playing guitar]

00:03:00.713 --> 00:03:06.118
(SINGING) It was born
of blood and war.

00:03:06.185 --> 00:03:10.890
Half ax, yet have sword.

00:03:10.956 --> 00:03:15.828
You'll surely lop off your head.

00:03:15.895 --> 00:03:19.465
I just made me a falchion.

00:03:21.834 --> 00:03:22.602
There she is.

00:03:22.702 --> 00:03:24.137
A blade has been born.

00:03:24.204 --> 00:03:27.006
That blade came out super
straight as an arrow.

00:03:27.106 --> 00:03:28.373
Fantastic.

00:03:28.474 --> 00:03:30.910
Looks like those candles
and all the stuff we did,

00:03:31.010 --> 00:03:31.844
sure enough worked.

00:03:35.314 --> 00:03:36.982 line:0%
MARK: The morning
of day two, and I'm

00:03:37.083 --> 00:03:38.718 line:0%
going to start on
my cross guard.

00:03:38.818 --> 00:03:42.055
I only have one piece of brass
that I can try this with.

00:03:42.155 --> 00:03:44.457
So I'm hoping to get it
right on the first try.

00:03:44.523 --> 00:03:46.826
The fittings are a huge part
of this and getting all of that

00:03:46.926 --> 00:03:50.463
to just really fit tightly,
snugly, be comfortable

00:03:50.530 --> 00:03:53.065
in the hand is going to
be hopefully where I'm

00:03:53.131 --> 00:03:56.802
able to win this competition.

00:03:56.869 --> 00:04:00.172 line:7%
Should be good enough.

00:04:00.273 --> 00:04:01.607 line:7%
 Let's do this.

00:04:01.674 --> 00:04:03.542
Feeling good about the
blade going in the last day.

00:04:03.642 --> 00:04:05.678
My only concern is
just getting the weight

00:04:05.745 --> 00:04:06.312
where it needs to be.

00:04:06.412 --> 00:04:07.713
It's a little bit heavy.

00:04:07.780 --> 00:04:09.983
I went ahead and decided,
we're going for fuller.

00:04:13.319 --> 00:04:15.188
I don't have a whole
lot of time left.

00:04:15.288 --> 00:04:17.189
I'm going to have to be
very strategic in everything

00:04:17.256 --> 00:04:19.324
I do today.

00:04:19.391 --> 00:04:20.526
I feel so accomplished.

00:04:20.592 --> 00:04:22.394
You know, for four
days, pulling off

00:04:22.461 --> 00:04:25.464
a blade this big with
the Damascus pattern,

00:04:25.564 --> 00:04:27.299
with the fit and
finish that I on it,

00:04:27.366 --> 00:04:28.401
I couldn't be any happier.

00:04:32.271 --> 00:04:33.739 line:0%
 It's the dawn
of the final day.

00:04:33.839 --> 00:04:36.675
I was able to get the blade
quenched and tempered.

00:04:36.775 --> 00:04:37.677
Perfect.

00:04:37.743 --> 00:04:42.548
Now it's time to
grind, shape, and glue.

00:04:42.615 --> 00:04:47.019
This has been a bunch of firsts
for me, first on length, first

00:04:47.119 --> 00:04:49.321
on a guard, first on a pommel.

00:04:49.388 --> 00:04:51.456
It's just non-stop firsts.

00:04:51.557 --> 00:04:53.826
I know that there are
some steps that I rushed.

00:04:53.893 --> 00:04:56.763
But for a four-day build,
I'm pretty happy with this.

00:04:59.232 --> 00:05:04.336
 All right, bladesmiths,
this is the kill test.

00:05:04.436 --> 00:05:05.838
To find out what
kind of lethal damage

00:05:05.904 --> 00:05:08.407
your weapon will do according
to its historic design,

00:05:08.473 --> 00:05:11.443
I will try to cut this
big carcass in half.

00:05:11.510 --> 00:05:12.978
Wayne, you are first.
Are you ready for this.

00:05:13.045 --> 00:05:13.879
 Absolutely.

00:05:13.946 --> 00:05:19.118
[metal music playing]

00:05:19.218 --> 00:05:19.985
 Oh man.

00:05:20.086 --> 00:05:21.254
 One and done.

00:05:21.354 --> 00:05:22.321
 Whoa now.

00:05:22.387 --> 00:05:23.522
 All right, Wayne.

00:05:23.589 --> 00:05:25.857
Your falchion is beautiful.

00:05:25.924 --> 00:05:27.427
It is sharp.

00:05:27.493 --> 00:05:29.628
And it cut through the spine
and all the way through the pig.

00:05:29.729 --> 00:05:32.264
It's a little bit heavier
for a one-handed weapon,

00:05:32.364 --> 00:05:34.200
but it is well balanced.

00:05:34.300 --> 00:05:37.036
Overall sir, it will kill.

00:05:37.136 --> 00:05:38.671
 Awesome.

00:05:38.771 --> 00:05:39.405
 All right, Mark.

00:05:39.472 --> 00:05:40.739
Your turn, sir.

00:05:40.840 --> 00:05:41.407
Are you ready?

00:05:41.507 --> 00:05:44.443
 Let's give it a shot.

00:05:44.510 --> 00:05:48.014
[metal music playing]

00:05:56.922 --> 00:05:58.024
 All right, Mark.

00:05:58.124 --> 00:05:59.124
Let's talk about
your falchion here.

00:05:59.224 --> 00:06:01.560
It's a nice, lighter blade.

00:06:01.627 --> 00:06:04.463
Your edges are sharp enough
to cut through spine.

00:06:04.529 --> 00:06:07.266
But the problem I have
here is your guard.

00:06:07.366 --> 00:06:09.602
Your edges here are not rounded.

00:06:09.668 --> 00:06:12.438
They dig in right here
where the thumb is.

00:06:12.505 --> 00:06:15.874
But your blade,
sir, it will kill.

00:06:15.974 --> 00:06:18.210
 Thank you.

00:06:18.277 --> 00:06:19.846
 All right gentlemen.

00:06:19.912 --> 00:06:21.881
To test the strength and overall
construction of your blades,

00:06:21.947 --> 00:06:24.750
I'll be attacking our
armored dummy here.

00:06:24.816 --> 00:06:28.687
This test is not about what
your swords do to that armor,

00:06:28.754 --> 00:06:31.256
it's about what that
armor does to your swords.

00:06:31.356 --> 00:06:32.024
Wayne, you're up.

00:06:32.091 --> 00:06:32.791
You ready?

00:06:32.892 --> 00:06:35.093
 Let's do it.

00:06:35.160 --> 00:06:38.064
[metal music playing]

00:06:47.640 --> 00:06:49.809
 Woo.

00:06:49.876 --> 00:06:53.345
 First off, Wayne, your edge
has taken some small chips

00:06:53.446 --> 00:06:54.613
and small rolls.

00:06:54.680 --> 00:06:56.415
But it's very,
very minor damage.

00:06:56.515 --> 00:06:58.217
There's still a sharp edge here.

00:06:58.317 --> 00:06:59.951
All in all, it held
up beautifully.

00:07:00.018 --> 00:07:00.720
 All right.

00:07:00.820 --> 00:07:01.386
Thank you.

00:07:01.453 --> 00:07:02.855
 So Mark, I got to ask.

00:07:02.922 --> 00:07:03.823
What's with the shirt?

00:07:03.923 --> 00:07:05.524
 I got married in
this shirt actually.

00:07:05.591 --> 00:07:08.060
It's, you know,
it's my formal wear.

00:07:08.127 --> 00:07:09.061
 All right.

00:07:09.161 --> 00:07:09.828
Well, you ready for the test?

00:07:09.928 --> 00:07:10.663
 I am.

00:07:10.730 --> 00:07:12.264
 OK.

00:07:12.331 --> 00:07:14.801
[metal music playing]

00:07:25.478 --> 00:07:27.379
 Not bad.

00:07:27.446 --> 00:07:28.614
 All right.

00:07:28.714 --> 00:07:31.316
So first off, the
blade is still solid.

00:07:31.416 --> 00:07:33.218
You did get some minor rolling.

00:07:33.318 --> 00:07:36.388
But the blade still has an edge.

00:07:36.455 --> 00:07:37.957
Down here's the problem.

00:07:38.023 --> 00:07:43.896
Your guard, these edges are
not just square, they're sharp.

00:07:43.963 --> 00:07:45.398
But the blade held up.

00:07:45.498 --> 00:07:46.131
Good job.

00:07:46.198 --> 00:07:47.299
 Thank you.

00:07:47.366 --> 00:07:48.968
 All right,
bladesmiths, now it's

00:07:49.035 --> 00:07:51.303
time to find out if there's any
sharpness left to your weapons.

00:07:51.370 --> 00:07:52.938
To test the edge
of your weapon, I'm

00:07:53.005 --> 00:07:57.175
going to cut through this
gauntlet of sandbags.

00:07:57.242 --> 00:07:58.010
Wayne, you are first.

00:07:58.077 --> 00:07:58.844
You ready for this?

00:07:58.911 --> 00:08:01.046
 Oh, yeah.

00:08:01.113 --> 00:08:05.551
[metal music playing]

00:08:16.295 --> 00:08:17.195
 All right, Wayne.

00:08:17.262 --> 00:08:18.697
Your weapon is sharp.

00:08:18.797 --> 00:08:22.100
On every swing, it cuts
and slashes nicely.

00:08:22.200 --> 00:08:27.807
And most importantly, aside
from being smurfed, it will cut.

00:08:27.907 --> 00:08:28.707
 Awesome.

00:08:28.774 --> 00:08:30.076
 All right, Mark,
it's your turn.

00:08:30.176 --> 00:08:31.310
You ready?
- I am.

00:08:31.377 --> 00:08:32.044
MAN: Let's have fun.

00:08:35.014 --> 00:08:38.284
[metal music playing]

00:08:49.628 --> 00:08:51.063
 All right, Mark.

00:08:51.129 --> 00:08:53.566
As you can see, on both of
these bags, it cut deeply.

00:08:53.633 --> 00:08:55.834
On the second bag, on the
swing back over there,

00:08:55.934 --> 00:08:57.637
it must have hit a dull spot.

00:08:57.737 --> 00:09:01.106
It did rip parts of the bag, but
it didn't cut all the way in.

00:09:01.173 --> 00:09:04.076
But overall, it is
sharp, and it will cut.

00:09:04.176 --> 00:09:06.512
 Yeah.

00:09:06.579 --> 00:09:09.549
WIL WILLIS: Wayne, Mark,
it was a tight decision.

00:09:13.185 --> 00:09:14.287
Wayne, congratulations.

00:09:14.353 --> 00:09:16.054
You're the "Forged
in Fire" champion.

00:09:16.154 --> 00:09:19.091
Mark, unfortunately, your
blade didn't make the cut.

00:09:19.191 --> 00:09:22.027
 Now, Mark, you made good
blades, no doubt about that.

00:09:22.127 --> 00:09:24.062
But the big problem
is mainly your guard.

00:09:24.162 --> 00:09:26.799
Not rounding off those
sections, those sharp corners

00:09:26.865 --> 00:09:28.767
will bite into the user's hand.

00:09:28.834 --> 00:09:30.602
And if a weapon's
going to hurt a user,

00:09:30.669 --> 00:09:32.638
they're not going to use it.

00:09:32.738 --> 00:09:36.375
 Please surrender your
weapon and leave the forge.

00:09:36.475 --> 00:09:38.110
MARK: From start to
finish, this whole thing

00:09:38.177 --> 00:09:40.312
was a learning process
for me, and I honestly

00:09:40.379 --> 00:09:44.683
think I have gotten years worth
of experience and feedback

00:09:44.750 --> 00:09:46.218
in just a short time.

00:09:46.319 --> 00:09:47.352
- Great job, man.
- [inaudible]

00:09:47.419 --> 00:09:48.520
 You, too.

00:09:48.587 --> 00:09:51.257
 This experience
was life-changing.

00:09:53.926 --> 00:09:56.596
 Wayne,
congratulations, you are

00:09:56.662 --> 00:10:01.066
one badass, everlasting
bladesmith and our new "Forged

00:10:01.166 --> 00:10:01.968
in Fire" champion.

00:10:02.034 --> 00:10:03.001
Good job, brother.

00:10:03.101 --> 00:10:03.836
 Yeah!

00:10:03.903 --> 00:10:04.536
Yes!

00:10:04.603 --> 00:10:05.503
 [chuckles]

00:10:05.570 --> 00:10:07.006
WAYNE: Yeah!

00:10:07.106 --> 00:10:10.542
 Please, at this time, present
your blade to our judges.

00:10:10.643 --> 00:10:11.610
 So I did it!

00:10:11.676 --> 00:10:13.112
Man, I wanted it!

00:10:13.212 --> 00:10:15.580
Next for me, I'm going to get
back on the same thing that's

00:10:15.647 --> 00:10:17.583
led me to this
point, which is just

00:10:17.649 --> 00:10:19.384
non-stop going full throttle.

00:10:19.485 --> 00:10:21.220
And I'm just going
to keep pushing.

00:10:21.287 --> 00:10:23.154
I'm going to keep [inaudible]
better and better.

00:10:23.255 --> 00:10:26.726
[music playing]

